<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="S5.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Interpolation of the scaling factors of <math id="S5.F6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{id}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{id}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.F6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{shape}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>shape</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{shape}}</annotation></semantics></math>. From left to right, the scaling factor of <math id="S5.F6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{id}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{id}}</annotation></semantics></math> linearly decreases from 2 to 0, while that of <math id="S5.F6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{shape}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>shape</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{shape}}</annotation></semantics></math> linearly increases from 0 to 2. The results in the middle match our default setting.</span></figcaption>
