<section id="Sx7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">F. Face Reconstruction Capability</h2>

<div id="Sx7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the identity preserving capability of our model, we perform face reconstruction for all identities in WebCaricature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, using the lowest-indexed photo as the ID image and extracting its edge map or landmarks as shape conditions. We use the cosine similarity of ArcFace <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> features as an additional metric. As shown in Table <a href="#Sx7.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ F. Face Reconstruction Capability ‣ CaricHarmony: Contrastive Diffusion Paths for Identity-Preserving Caricature Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, our method achieves a significantly higher ArcFace similarity and a competitive I-CLIP score compared to modern caricature synthesis models, demonstrating that our method can effectively preserve facial features of identities.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx7.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="Sx7.T5.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="Sx7.T5.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Sx7.T5.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Methods</td>
<td id="Sx7.T5.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">I-CLIP <math id="Sx7.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="Sx7.T5.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">ArcFace-sim <math id="Sx7.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="Sx7.T5.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
